    {
      "id": "47b72ab9-fa03-4e15-83bb-39c8faad7a3b",
      "name": "Ingress Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1900,
        "height": 280,
        "content": "## Webhook Ingress\n\nMechanics only; names come from the config key. The webhook secret is read from the configured Redis key at request time and is never stored in this workflow.\n\nVerify the HMAC signature of the raw body (401 on mismatch, fail-closed when the secret is unset). Normalize the GitHub payload into the intake envelope; check events (check_run / workflow_run) are normalized to the pull request they ran for. Admit only configured events; bot actors are admitted for opened/reopened/closed and for check events, so the pipeline's own label edits cannot loop.\n\nRouting after admission, in order: a failed counted check (a required context or one of `ci.checks`) on a pipeline PR becomes a repair item (stage repair, deduped per head SHA and check); a merged pull request on a pipeline branch labels its issue shipped; review feedback from an approver becomes a feedback item; an approving review calls the merger immediately; everything else goes to the intake queue in the poller's item shape."
      }
    },
